WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.980
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.450
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.360 --> 00:32.260
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.660 --> 00:40.760
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.460
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.460 --> 00:50.860
What should I believe?

00:51.360 --> 00:59.860
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.260 --> 01:08.860
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.060 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:35.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs

01:42.360 --> 01:48.590
I was a foundling who was rescued from a slave dealer by the traveling artist, Vitalis.

01:49.340 --> 01:50.340
On that day,

01:50.530 --> 01:55.290
I had to say goodbye to my dear mother and begin my endless journey.

01:57.000 --> 02:02.000
Episode 5:
Miracle of the St. Maria Statue

02:04.460 --> 02:06.670
We'll take a little rest.
- Okay

02:17.360 --> 02:19.100
Wow, that's cold.

02:28.560 --> 02:30.210
Got it!

02:30.540 --> 02:32.480
Give it back!

02:34.070 --> 02:35.870
I said, give it back!

02:39.930 --> 02:40.940
Give it back!

02:43.570 --> 02:45.350
Hey, get down!

02:49.890 --> 02:50.800
Watch out!

02:54.340 --> 02:55.250
Remy!

03:00.430 --> 03:01.600
Are you all right?

03:05.780 --> 03:07.940
Is anything broken?

03:08.340 --> 03:10.810
It must've been those brats from the orphanage.

03:11.560 --> 03:13.720
They're known to love causing mischief.

03:28.270 --> 03:29.390
There we go.

03:30.490 --> 03:32.090
Thank you.
- How is it?

03:32.170 --> 03:33.860
It doesn't hurt anymore.

03:36.220 --> 03:38.780
We're really sorry for what happened.

03:40.190 --> 03:41.120
It's all right.

03:48.060 --> 03:49.430
Sorry.

03:50.900 --> 03:51.830
Nina...

03:54.030 --> 03:55.510
Why is she crying?

03:55.970 --> 04:01.420
Nina is Pierre's sister.
I hope you can forgive her brother.

04:04.790 --> 04:09.530
Nina, please don't cry.
- Pierre, this is your fault.

04:09.990 --> 04:12.370
I know. I'll apologise.

04:15.550 --> 04:16.730
Sorry for earlier.

04:17.380 --> 04:18.350
It's all right.

04:27.670 --> 04:31.840
Look, she's fine, right?
You don't have to worry about her, Nina.

04:32.340 --> 04:33.180
Pierre!

04:35.300 --> 04:38.620
He really is a troublemaker.

04:40.010 --> 04:43.300
He's a nuisance.
Yet, he's so kind to Nina.

04:51.470 --> 04:54.780
It seems Nina doesn't speak.

04:55.400 --> 04:56.940
Yes, that's right.

04:57.560 --> 05:00.330
She could speak before but suddenly...

05:01.550 --> 05:02.360
Suddenly?

05:03.160 --> 05:05.360
Her mother died.

05:05.930 --> 05:08.690
Since then she has not been able to say a word.

05:16.650 --> 05:17.550
Who's there?

05:18.430 --> 05:21.380
Hey, can the little monkey really act?

05:21.430 --> 05:22.570
Everyone.

05:22.660 --> 05:25.950
Mr. Vitalis, looks like a big audience.

05:26.980 --> 05:27.820
Mmhm.

05:30.160 --> 05:32.180
Seems like Joli-Coeur wants to show off his skills.

05:56.080 --> 06:03.130
Our next act is the play "Joli-Coeur's Servant".

06:11.950 --> 06:16.750
<i>She could speak before but suddenly, her mother died.</i>

06:16.860 --> 06:19.710
<i>Since then she has not been able to say a word.</i>

06:33.860 --> 06:34.830
Mother.

06:40.340 --> 06:43.250
Mother, I'm doing my best.

07:00.220 --> 07:01.120
Pierre?

07:15.800 --> 07:17.480
Who is it? Who's there?!

07:18.050 --> 07:20.010
I know you're there, come out!

07:24.820 --> 07:25.500
Remy.

07:26.120 --> 07:28.630
Sorry I scared you.

07:30.260 --> 07:34.380
Why are you following me?
- Where are you going at this hour?

07:35.570 --> 07:37.880
Shut up, I'm not telling you.

07:39.410 --> 07:42.140
I can only tell my friends at the orphanage.

07:42.910 --> 07:43.820
Why?

07:46.550 --> 07:48.870
They have no mothers or fathers.

07:49.660 --> 07:52.900
So they are my friends.
- Well, then I'm your friend too.

07:54.290 --> 07:57.040
I don't have a mother or father either.

07:59.580 --> 08:03.680
I do have a stepmother, she raised me as her own.

08:05.990 --> 08:07.870
I was a foundling.

08:09.100 --> 08:10.770
Really?

08:10.930 --> 08:15.450
Really. If it wasn't for Mr. Vitalis I would've been sold.

08:24.400 --> 08:25.610
I'll go back then.

08:26.420 --> 08:29.400
Wait! I understand.

08:31.820 --> 08:35.440
Follow me.
Just keep it secret from the adults.

08:35.950 --> 08:36.740
Mmhm.

08:49.550 --> 08:52.920
What is this place?
- Mr. Gerald's mansion.

08:53.510 --> 08:57.410
Mr. Gerald's...!?
We're sneaking into someone's house!?

08:58.360 --> 09:00.080
Shut up and follow me.

09:01.210 --> 09:03.340
No, we shouldn't!

09:05.310 --> 09:08.990
I know, but I have to do this for Nina.

09:10.400 --> 09:11.740
For Nina?

09:19.370 --> 09:20.290
This way.

09:42.620 --> 09:47.560
St. Maria, I beg you, please let Nina speak again.

09:48.460 --> 09:49.500
Pierre...

09:50.090 --> 09:52.850
You come here to pray for this.

09:54.990 --> 09:57.410
Tonight is the ninety-ninth day I've prayed for it.

09:57.960 --> 09:59.550
Ninety-ninth?

10:00.320 --> 10:04.690
My mother used to say that if you prayed for a hundred days straight,

10:05.040 --> 10:08.480
St. Maria will perform a miracle.

10:08.760 --> 10:13.090
Nina loved that story.
She always asked mom to tell it.

10:16.370 --> 10:20.890
<i>Hey, mom, tell us the usual story about St. Maria.</i>

10:22.470 --> 10:23.520
<i>All right, all right.</i>

10:26.330 --> 10:31.200
A long time ago, there was a village where a kind-hearted girl lived.

10:32.190 --> 10:37.020
The girl's grandmother was suffering from a long-term illness.

10:38.100 --> 10:40.710
The girl prayed everyday.

10:41.250 --> 10:45.020
"Make grandmother's illness go away soon."

10:52.050 --> 10:54.260
On exactly the hundredth day,

10:55.690 --> 10:59.590
St. Maria approached the girl and said:

11:01.470 --> 11:04.040
"I came to answer your prayers."

11:06.450 --> 11:10.300
She restored the girl's grandmother's health.

11:10.590 --> 11:14.560
Did St. Maria really come down?
- Did she really perform a miracle?

11:15.420 --> 11:20.620
Yes, St. Maria is always a friend to the small and weak.

11:23.440 --> 11:26.350
Soon after, my mother died.

11:26.920 --> 11:29.440
From that day on, Nina wouldn't speak.

11:32.410 --> 11:34.700
Tomorrow is the last of the hundred days.

11:35.610 --> 11:39.130
For Nina, St. Maria, I ask you to perform this miracle.

11:40.320 --> 11:43.280
Nina must speak again.

11:58.490 --> 12:01.930
What did you say? Pierre is...
- Yes.

12:02.400 --> 12:05.400
Look at the child-sized footprints.

12:06.070 --> 12:09.400
And it seems like there are two children.
- Two?

12:09.710 --> 12:12.200
Pierre and who else?

12:12.400 --> 12:13.340
I don't know.

12:13.410 --> 12:17.800
But it seems that boy Pierre has been sneaking out every night.

12:18.020 --> 12:19.670
Every night? Every night!

12:21.650 --> 12:23.610
So, what'd he steal?

12:23.990 --> 12:26.110
I'm not sure at this point.

12:26.500 --> 12:29.240
But if we asked, we'd have the answer.

12:29.590 --> 12:33.760
Bring him to me immediately.
I will check the house.

12:33.790 --> 12:34.980
Certainly.

12:45.080 --> 12:47.330
They get inside from here.

12:47.750 --> 12:49.450
What an annoying brat.

12:55.440 --> 12:59.370
Today's finally the hundredth day.
- Shh! Don't be so loud!

13:00.800 --> 13:01.990
Sorry.

13:03.160 --> 13:05.930
But it's really great, every day, without fail.

13:06.240 --> 13:07.850
Good job, Pierre!

13:09.150 --> 13:09.950
It's nothing.

13:10.830 --> 13:14.600
But, will the miracle really happen?
- It will!

13:14.990 --> 13:17.700
Nina will be able to speak again.

13:46.180 --> 13:49.670
Pierre, promise me you won't-
- I know.

13:49.930 --> 13:53.990
After today, I won't be sneaking into Gerald's mansion.

13:54.030 --> 13:55.260
Sneaking into?

13:56.410 --> 13:59.140
Pierre, it really is you.

14:00.600 --> 14:06.200
Pierre, you really go into Gerald's home every night to steal?

14:07.080 --> 14:08.730
No!
- Come here!

14:09.410 --> 14:15.890
I won't let Pierre go out tonight, I'll watch him. So, please, forgive him.

14:18.670 --> 14:19.380
Wait!

14:26.560 --> 14:29.380
Hey! Wait, Pierre!

14:37.830 --> 14:42.430
Only one more! I just have to pray once more and then there will be a miracle.

14:42.570 --> 14:44.900
If I don't go now, I'll never get a chance.

14:52.660 --> 14:53.850
St. Maria...

15:00.460 --> 15:05.000
<i>I have to get there, where St. Maria... where St. Maria is.</i>

15:16.330 --> 15:20.010
Why is there smoke?
- Somebody!

15:33.900 --> 15:34.890
Mr. Gerald!

15:41.090 --> 15:42.430
Such thick smoke!

15:43.690 --> 15:44.770
Pierre!

15:51.070 --> 15:51.910
Pierre...

15:55.100 --> 15:56.230
Pierre, hurry!

16:01.280 --> 16:03.500
Damn... This way, Remy, hurry!

16:08.180 --> 16:09.650
The house is on fire!?

16:09.870 --> 16:13.770
Yes, everyone is trying to save him but the fire is growing.

16:14.150 --> 16:15.340
Mr. Gerald!

16:16.440 --> 16:17.940
What's wrong, Nina?

16:20.890 --> 16:22.920
What, what do you want to say?

16:23.300 --> 16:27.150
Pierre must be in that house.
- And Remy too.

16:28.700 --> 16:29.560
Remy!

16:36.040 --> 16:39.720
The master's in danger! Hurry and put the fire out! Hurry!

16:42.690 --> 16:45.620
Capi, wait here with everyone.

16:54.460 --> 16:56.360
Remy, get a hold of yourself!

16:56.380 --> 16:58.890
Hurry and escape!
- Okay.

17:00.150 --> 17:03.900
Remy, Pierre, where are you!?

17:07.290 --> 17:08.880
Remy, Pierre!

17:10.510 --> 17:11.430
Remy!

17:13.000 --> 17:14.170
Mr. Vitalis!

17:14.590 --> 17:15.620
Remy, Pierre!

17:16.130 --> 17:17.410
Mr. Vitalis!

17:17.540 --> 17:19.850
Thank goodness. Are you all right?
- Yes.

17:20.870 --> 17:21.850
Good, let's go.

17:28.890 --> 17:30.170
Hang in there, Pierre.

17:44.390 --> 17:45.950
Remy, where are you going?

17:46.280 --> 17:48.380
You guys go ahead!
- Remy!

18:02.280 --> 18:04.180
Master!
- Pierre!

18:12.230 --> 18:13.480
Remy's still inside.

18:23.070 --> 18:24.880
I'm sorry, Nina.

18:34.400 --> 18:35.080
Remy!

18:35.770 --> 18:36.930
Wait, it's dangerous!

18:37.020 --> 18:40.880
Remy's still in there and St. Maria's gonna be burned!

18:41.250 --> 18:43.570
I come here to pray for Nina!

18:44.410 --> 18:45.990
For Nina?

18:46.370 --> 18:49.010
Remy! St. Maria!

18:59.900 --> 19:03.560
That was foolish.
- I'm sorry. I won't do it again.

19:08.430 --> 19:09.920
Remy!

19:10.400 --> 19:13.920
You saved me along with Pierre.

19:15.380 --> 19:16.320
Thank you.

19:16.960 --> 19:19.140
Pierre was really brave.

19:19.320 --> 19:25.600
Yes, but I didn't know that troublesome boy was coming to pray for his sister.

19:25.840 --> 19:29.940
Had he told me, I would've given him the St. Maria statue as a present.

19:30.650 --> 19:32.500
Would you really do that?

19:40.130 --> 19:41.540
Guess I'll have to start anew.

19:42.290 --> 19:44.890
We'll find another St. Maria statue and pray to it.

19:45.370 --> 19:46.960
And soon it'll be a hundred days.

19:50.440 --> 19:51.900
What is it, Nina?

20:03.100 --> 20:07.720
St. Maria, why is she here?

20:15.730 --> 20:18.040
<i>On exactly the hundredth day,</i>

20:19.360 --> 20:23.330
<i>St. Maria approached the girl and said:</i>

20:25.140 --> 20:27.720
"I came to answer your prayers."

20:33.340 --> 20:35.720
St. Maria.

20:39.270 --> 20:42.590
St. Maria is here.

20:47.270 --> 20:51.810
Nina, you... spoke.

20:55.530 --> 20:56.900
Brother.

21:04.500 --> 21:06.580
Nina, say it again.

21:07.190 --> 21:08.120
Brother.

21:11.780 --> 21:12.700
Nina!

21:15.990 --> 21:21.190
It's just like mother said.
It's just like she said.

21:22.000 --> 21:25.180
Yes, that's right.

21:37.100 --> 21:45.280
Try to love yourself more

21:46.730 --> 21:55.760
Abandoned dreams can be seen again

21:56.310 --> 22:04.570
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

22:05.950 --> 22:16.800
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

22:17.370 --> 22:27.030
Tomorrow's courage comes

22:27.230 --> 22:36.850
From the future that gives us our fate

22:37.080 --> 22:45.300
Try to seek for them more

22:46.750 --> 22:50.340
Give your heart to

22:50.660 --> 23:03.680
That person who is also seeking you

23:17.930 --> 23:20.270
That person is Ms. Ivonne.

23:21.390 --> 23:25.580
Sarah, where is my real mother?

23:27.480 --> 23:28.980
That Mrs. Ivonne...?

23:29.660 --> 23:31.080
Move forward, Remy.

23:31.490 --> 23:32.930
Look towards tomorrow.

23:32.950 --> 23:36.440
<i>Mother's Phantom</i>

23:32.950 --> 23:36.440
Next time:
